================================================================================
EXERCISE 3: BRANCHING & MERGING - LAB EXECUTION LOG
================================================================================

Step 1: Initial Repository & Master Branch Setup
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Initialize repository:
   $ git init
   Initialized empty Git repository in Ex3_BranchingAndMerging/Code/.git/

2. Create initial file and commit on master:
   $ "Initial master branch content." | Out-File -FilePath main.txt
   $ git add main.txt
   $ git commit -m "Initial commit on master branch"
   [master (root-commit) 1fec7a0] Initial commit on master branch
    1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

Step 2: Branching
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Create new branch `GitNewBranch`:
   $ git branch GitNewBranch

2. List all branches (before switch):
   $ git branch -a
     GitNewBranch
   * master

3. Switch to `GitNewBranch`:
   $ git checkout GitNewBranch
   Switched to branch 'GitNewBranch'

4. List all branches (after switch):
   $ git branch -a
   * GitNewBranch
     master

5. Add file and commit to `GitNewBranch`:
   $ "Feature implementation in GitNewBranch." | Out-File -FilePath feature.txt
   $ git add feature.txt
   $ git commit -m "Add feature.txt to GitNewBranch"
   [GitNewBranch 1a8ad6a] Add feature.txt to GitNewBranch
    1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

6. Check status:
   $ git status
   On branch GitNewBranch
   nothing to commit, working tree clean

Step 3: Merging
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Switch back to `master`:
   $ git checkout master
   Switched to branch 'master'

2. List out CLI differences between master and GitNewBranch:
   $ git diff master GitNewBranch
   diff --git a/feature.txt b/feature.txt
   new file mode 100644
   --- /dev/null
   +++ b/feature.txt
   @@ -0,0 +1 @@
   +Feature implementation in GitNewBranch.

3. Merge `GitNewBranch` into `master`:
   $ git merge GitNewBranch
   Updating 1fec7a0..1a8ad6a
   Fast-forward
    feature.txt | 1 +
    1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
    create mode 100644 feature.txt

4. Observe graph log after merging:
   $ git log --oneline --graph --decorate
   * 1a8ad6a (HEAD -> master, GitNewBranch) Add feature.txt to GitNewBranch
   * 1fec7a0 Initial commit on master branch

5. Delete branch `GitNewBranch`:
   $ git branch -d GitNewBranch
   Deleted branch GitNewBranch (was 1a8ad6a).

6. Verify status and branches after deletion:
   $ git status
   On branch master
   nothing to commit, working tree clean

   $ git branch -a
   * master

